      "leadSummary": "Transcription is not a single instantaneous event. Promoter recognition, initiation, elongation, RNA processing and termination have different kinetics and may respond differently to regulators. Regulatory binding provides an input state, but RNA synthesis is an output that must be measured separately. In bacteria, the"
