          "secNumber": "5.8",
          "heading": "Unit-specific integrated assessment",
          "content": "RNA processing can be assessed by assigning four groups of junction reads to two imaginary tissues, each with different RNA-extraction yields. Students calculate isoform proportions and then notice that the proportions do not reveal how many transcripts were present originally. Add a pre-mRNA assay to estimate synthesis and a pulse-chase experiment to estimate degradation of the mature isoforms. One group may exhibit a high inclusion fraction simply because the skipping isoform decays rapidly. Learners must also decide how to verify an apparent A-to-I editing site using matched genomic DNA and mapping-quality checks. No single RNA-sequencing track can settle all of these questions. The design rewards appropriate complementary measurements and careful reference annotations rather than sheer sequencing depth.",
