          "secNumber": "7.7",
          "heading": "Unit synthesis",
          "content": "Gene-regulatory systems connect physical DNA packaging with dynamic networks and environmentally dependent decisions. The question is not whether a histone mark is associated with an active gene but whether a controlled perturbation of the mark changes the proposed causal pathway. A small circuit may be represented by a negative-feedback equation whose final output is easy to calculate, yet this equation does not specify the timescale on which regulation responds. Design a time-course after an environmental pulse and predict how an open-loop and a feedback-containing variant might differ. Distinguish direct perturbation effects from altered cell proportions when the whole population is sampled. To discuss epigenetic memory, define how many divisions the state must persist and whether the underlying DNA sequence remains unchanged.",
